It is evening and I am in the flat.
Someone knocks on the door.
It is my neighbour Sabine with her small dog Bruno.
"Happy birthday, Maya!" says Sabine.
She gives me a small houseplant.
I thank her and invite her in.
We sit by the open window.
The evening breeze is very warm.
Bruno sleeps on the floor.
"How was your day at the office?" Sabine asks.
"Did you have a good time?"
"Yes, my day was fantastic," I answer.
"I had a great morning."
"My colleagues organised a small surprise."
"We ate cake together."
"I really had no idea."
"That sounds lovely," says Sabine and smiles.
I am very happy about the visit.
